Hi Folks,

I spent the last week on getting the RFCOMM service level security fully
and also correctly working on SMP and Hyperthreading machines. The main
problem was that the fix for the socket unlink race contains a deadlock
and this was not really obvious. However this problem should now be
fixed and the service level security for RFCOMM should work. The code is
in patch-2.6.10-mh2 and I expect some test reports before I am going to
merge this finally back into the mainline kernel.

Regards

Marcel




